[perf] @kda_sub2_score_stable_kernel.vec #164 repo/kernels/projects/a5/kda_fwd_stable/kernels/intra.py:238:16: warning: ub_to_l1.nd2nz composes multiple MTE3 bursts (one per NZ fractal column of the ND rows) — not a single instruction, and board-measured 10x slower than the compact-NZ move (D-084); store the tile as compact NZ from the @vf instead (a strided vf.store writes the fractal directly) and move it with the plain ub_to_l1. WHEN YOU DO: pad the staging tile by one row so that store's block stride is ODD. The natural stride is the tile's row count, which is 16-aligned by nature and so is the worst rung of the bank ladder (~8.7 cycles a store against ~1.1, D-084) — on the two kernels reworked in D-226 the padding was worth MORE than this move is (-12.3 and -10.8 us of -17.7 and -28.2), and it is worth taking blind: one UB row, and it only ever costs nothing when the store pipe is idle anyway
